  "reference_expectations": [
    "Schema checks candidate shapes only. Signature verification, current authorization, target allowlists, UTF-8 byte budgets and actual HTTP behavior require implementation tests.",
    "The fixed POST routes below are metadata, not a running mock server or mandatory company adapter URLs. Query selectors belong in the signed body; its receipt must match the locally frozen delivery/profile/payload hash.",
    "Hash only the 12 hash_reference.projection_fields from the first frozen SendRequest. Use deterministic sorted-key JSON and UTF-8, preserve exact subject/body, reject duplicate keys and lone surrogates, never trim or normalize Unicode. Exclude schema_version wrapper, payload_sha256, idempotency_key, signatures and attempt/transport data. Schema cannot recompute or prove this hash.",
    "SEND-FROZEN-PAYLOAD includes a composed subject character, decomposed body character, newline and trailing space. Its hash is externally recomputed; changing profile, recipient or content requires an independent authorized replacement delivery.",
    "The provider fixture must retain (profile,idempotency_key): same payload returns the original receipt; different payload returns 409 without another effect. No vector or shape validation proves that storage or idempotency behavior.",
    "Accept-then-disconnect, query after core restart, unsupported-query profiles and unknown quarantine need a real fixture/process journey. Transport failure after possible acceptance means unknown, never confirmed no effect.",
    "Callbacks deduplicate by trusted provider source plus provider_event_id and CAS local revision after delivery/profile/hash binding. Wrong bindings or unknown providers are quarantined; late accepted cannot regress delivered. These are reference expectations, not schema-proven cross-field equality, event deduplication or state-machine tests.",
    "Only accepted/delivered/rejected/unknown are public receipt states; delivered requires real provider evidence. Legacy nil error or sent is not delivery proof. retry_class uses the existing common enum; valid shapes do not authorize retry or prove a state/retry combination.",
    "rule_version is a positive safe integer, matching existing rule-version DTOs; 64-bit IDs/revisions retain their own string contracts. This selected mock does not redefine the subscription DTO."
  ],
